\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 1}
The sums are
\[
\sum x=101,\quad \sum y=198,\quad \sum x^2=1141,\quad \sum y^2=4464,\quad \sum xy=2251.
\]
Thus
\[
\bar x=10.1,\quad \bar y=19.8,
\]
\[
V(x)=1141/10-10.1^2=\boxed{12.09},\quad V(y)=4464/10-19.8^2=\boxed{54.36},
\]
\[
\sigma_x=3.477,\quad \sigma_y=7.373,
\]
\[
Cov(x,y)=2251/10-(10.1)(19.8)=\boxed{25.12},
\]
\[
R=25.12/(3.477\times7.373)=\boxed{0.9799}.
\]
Since $|R|\ge 0.86$, the course classifies this as a good positive linear correlation.
\[
a=25.12/12.09=2.07775,\quad b=19.8-2.07775(10.1)=-1.18528,
\]
so
\[
\boxed{\hat y=2.07775x-1.18528}.
\]
For 3000 customers, $x=30$: $\hat y=61.1472$, hence
\[
\boxed{611\,472\text{ euros approximately}}.
\]
\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 2}
$\bar t=5.5$, $V(t)=8.25$, $\sum tx=654$, so
\[
Cov(t,x)=654/10-(5.5)(10.1)=9.85,
\]
\[
R(t,x)=\boxed{0.9863}.
\]
\[
a=9.85/8.25=1.19394,\quad b=10.1-1.19394(5.5)=3.53333.
\]
Hence $\hat x=1.19394t+3.53333$. For $t=12$, $\hat x=17.8606$, about 1786 customers. Using the first regression, $\hat y=35.9246$, or about \boxed{359\,246 euros}.
\solution{Detailed solution -- Exercise 3}
\[
A=((1+2+3)/3,(7+10+10)/3)=(2,9),
\]
\[
B=((4+5)/2,(14+14)/2)=(4.5,14).
\]
The slope is $(14-9)/(4.5-2)=2$ and the intercept is 5. Therefore the Mayer line is
\[
\boxed{y=2x+5}.
\]

